For a mini-batch, PyTorch reduces each head loss by dividing the summed weighted contributions by the sum of the corresponding target-class weights. Thus, for the valid examples \(\mathcal{B}_a\) of attribute \(a\),

\begin{equation}
\overline{\mathcal{L}}_a = \frac{\sum_{j\in\mathcal{B}_a}-w_{a,y_{a,j}}\log p_{a,j,y_{a,j}}}{\sum_{j\in\mathcal{B}_a}w_{a,y_{a,j}}}.
\end{equation}

\noindent The overall optimisation objective is the unweighted sum of these four reduced attribute losses:

old:
\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{angle}}
+
\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{mounting}}
+
\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{condition}}
+
\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{shape}}.

new:
\overline{\mathcal{L}}_{\mathrm{angle}}
+\overline{\mathcal{L}}_{\mathrm{mounting}}
+\overline{\mathcal{L}}_{\mathrm{condition}}
+\overline{\mathcal{L}}_{\mathrm{shape}}.
